## 2. Infrastructure — $170K to $240K (20%)

### Cloud Hosting (AWS) — $48K to $72K

| Service | Purpose | Monthly Cost | Annual Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| EC2 Instances | Application servers (web and API layers) | $1,500–$2,500 | $18K–$30K |
| RDS Database | PostgreSQL for user data, recipes, stores | $800–$1,200 | $9.6K–$14.4K |
| ElastiCache | Redis for caching and session management | $300–$500 | $3.6K–$6K |
| Lambda Functions | Serverless for image processing, notifications | $200–$400 | $2.4K–$4.8K |
| Load Balancers | Traffic distribution and high availability | $400–$600 | $4.8K–$7.2K |
| Auto-scaling | Handle traffic spikes from viral recipes | $800–$1,200 | $9.6K–$14.4K |

Growth assumption: starts at ~$2K/month during Q1–Q2 and scales to ~$6K/month by Q4 as the user base grows from 500 to 15,000.

### CDN (Content Delivery Network) — $24K to $48K

Video-first platforms are bandwidth-heavy. Cost scales with user growth:

| Period | Users | Bandwidth | Quarterly Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| Month 1–3 | 500 | 2 TB/month | $240 |
| Month 4–6 | 2,000 | 8 TB/month | $960 |
| Month 7–9 | 4,000 | 15 TB/month | $1,800 |
| Month 10–12 | 5,000 | 20 TB/month | $2,400 |

The budget is set higher ($24K–$48K) as a safety margin to absorb viral traffic spikes (a single trending recipe can cause 10x normal traffic), multiple video quality levels (480p, 720p, 1080p), and geographic expansion requiring additional edge locations.

### Storage (S3/Blob) — $12K to $24K

| Type | Purpose | Year 1 Volume | Annual Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| Video Storage | Recipe videos on S3 | 5–10 TB | $1.4K–$2.8K |
| Image Storage | User profiles, food photos | 500 GB–1 TB | $132–$276 |
| Database Backups | Automated backups, disaster recovery | 200–500 GB | $60–$144 |
| Thumbnail Cache | Video thumbnails for fast feed loading | 100–200 GB | $36–$60 |

Growth model assumes 100 new recipe videos per month in Q1–Q2, scaling to 500 per month by Q3–Q4, totaling approximately 3,000 videos (5–10 TB including CDN cache copies) by end of year.

### Database and Analytics — $12K to $24K

| Service | Purpose | Annual Cost |
|---|---|---|
| PostgreSQL (primary DB) | Recipes, users, stores, orders | $4.8K–$9.6K |
| Mixpanel or Amplitude | Product analytics and user behavior | $2.4K–$4.8K |
| BigQuery | Data warehouse for reporting | $1.8K–$3.6K |
| Datadog or New Relic | Infrastructure monitoring and alerting | $3K–$6K |

### Development Tools and Licenses — $15K to $25K

Covers GitHub Enterprise ($2.1K), Figma Professional ($1.8K), Jira/Linear ($1.2K), Slack Business ($1.4K), Postman ($600), Sentry for error tracking ($1.2K), SendGrid for transactional email ($1.2K), Twilio for SMS verification ($1.2K), OpenAI APIs for dietary filtering planned in Q3 ($2.4K), and miscellaneous SaaS tools ($2K).

### Security and Compliance — $20K to $30K

| Category | Purpose | Annual Cost |
|---|---|---|
| FERPA Compliance Audit | Student data protection review (legally required) | $5K–$10K |
| Penetration Testing | Security audits, twice per year | $8K–$12K |
| PCI-DSS Compliance | Payment security (Stripe handles most of it) | $2K |
| Bug Bounty Program | HackerOne or Bugcrowd | $2K–$4K |
| Cyber Insurance | Data breach insurance | $2.5K–$4K |
| SSL Certificates | HTTPS encryption | $500 |

FERPA compliance is non-negotiable when handling student data. Penetration testing prevents security breaches that could destroy user trust and shut down the company.

### API Integrations — $10K to $15K

Covers Stripe for payment processing ($3K–$5K at 2.9% + $0.30 per transaction), Google Maps API for store locations ($2.4K), Twilio SendGrid and SMS ($2.4K), OneSignal for push notifications ($600), Algolia for search ($1.2K), and Cloudinary for image optimization ($1.2K).

